   "raw": "id: 6\ndata: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"content\":\"Executing: WriteDocument\",\"metadata\":{\"tool\":\"WriteDocument\",\"toolInput\":{\"content\":\"# Line Edit Report — The Keeper's Arithmetic — Chapter 5 (Second Pass)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## FINDING SUMMARY\\n\\n| Finding | Severity | Category | Paragraph | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| None | — | — | — | Zero findings created |\\n\\n**Total findings: 0**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## CHAPTER 5 QUALITY ASSESSMENT\\n\\n### Overall prose quality: Excellent. Voice-calibrated and prose-clean.\\n\\nThis chapter maintains the maritime procedural register with surgical precision. All deviations flagged in the previous pass (ornamental sunset description, abstract vocabulary) have been resolved. The standing finding regarding the dangling modifier in paragraph 8 (\\\"Walking back up the steps, the lamp...\\\") is intentionally preserved per the writer's explicit style preference: *\\\"Preserve dangling modifiers that mimic cognitive slippage or fatigue.\\\"* This modifier now functions as a deliberate cognitive slippage — momentary inattention in a grieving narrator whose mind drifts from the action (walking) to the observation (lamp dimmer). **This is NOT an error.**\\n\\n### What this chapter does right:\\n\\n1. **Opening precision** — Paragraph 1 establishes immediate procedural observation. Subject-first declaratives (\\\"The skiff came ashore\\\"), physical detail anchored to action (\\\"rope had frayed where it crossed the iron ring\\\"), and emotional distance through log refusal (\\\"the log does not take opinions\\\") all arrive cleanly.\\n\\n2. **Weight-arithmetic extension** — \\\"The smaller arithmetic: the rope and the ring and the salt that held them together\\\" extends the weight/gravity metaphor domain through accumulated physical detail, not abstraction. This is voice-perfect.\\n\\n3. **The bill simile** — \\\"A boat with no oars arrives the way a bill arrives: someone else has already decided you owe.\\\" Correctly deploys the signature \\\"the way [verb]\\\" universalizing device. Thematic resonance (debt, obligation, enforced arrival) registers without naming it.\\n\\n4. **Chapter-closing symmetry** — \\\"Then I did not draw the line, because whoever emptied the tin was not finished, and neither was I.\\\" Creates exact procedural parallel with Chapter 4's \\\"Drew no line\\\" and the procedural rupture arc begun in Chapter 2 (wick not trimmed). The refusal-to-close mirrors open grief and open investigation.\\n\\n5. **Voice calibration maintained** — Zero ellipses, zero semicolons, em dashes at estimated 2 (within fingerprint range of 2.5–3), fragment-stacked mood setting (\\\"No oars. None.\\\"), log entries functioning as rhythm markers, compressed paradox (\\\"Two things true at once\\\") deployed correctly, inference-from-physical-detail (\\\"whoever tied them was in a hurry or in the dark\\\") as the narrator's core move.\\n\\n### Prose patterns to watch for:\\n\\n- **Density in recursive phrasing** — The sentence \\\"the tin I found wedged under the stone I had found the first letter under, weeks ago, when this was still a story about grief\\\" is syntactically complex and approaches the edge of reader-processing difficulty. However, this density functions intentionally: it tracks the narrator's mental recursion (present discovery → past discovery → earlier emotional state). The reader experiences the same cognitive stumble the narrator has. This is a voice choice, not an error.\\n\\n- **\\\"you could see it in how they had dried\\\"** — This inference construction is the narrator's protected core move, not a filter word. It works.\\n\\n- **\\\"properly\\\" as adverb** — \\\"looked at her properly\\\" carries nautical procedural meaning (examining with boat-person care, versus observing from the gallery). Not a weak adverb in this register.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## PROTECTED SIGNATURE DEVICES — OPERATING CORRECTLY\\n\\nThe following patterns appear in this chapter and are **intentional**, matching the style fingerprint:\\n\\n| Device | Occurrences | Fingerprint Status |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| \\\"the way [verb]\\\" universalizing | para 1, para 3 | Signature device |\\n| Fragment-stacked mood setting | para 3 (\\\"No oars. None.\\\"), para 6 (\\\"Barometer steady.\\\") | Deliberate fragment deployment |\\n| Log entry insertions | para 2, para 9 | Rhythm markers |\\n| Compressed paradox | para 5 (\\\"Two things true at once\\\") | Known signature |\\n| Weight metaphor accumulation | para 6 (\\\"smaller arithmetic\\\") | Extends weight/gravity domain |\\n| Displacement emotion through procedure | para 9 (\\\"did not draw the line\\\") | Primary emotion-rendering method |\\n| Dangling modifiers | para 8 | Writer preference: preserved for cognitive slippage |\\n| Inference from physical detail | para 4 (\\\"you could see it in how they had dried\\\") | Core move, not filter word |\\n| Time-markers as structural pivots | \\\"Tuesday,\\\" \\\"That night,\\\" \\\"Inside the tin\\\" | Deliberate pacing |\\n| Em dash for procedural interruption | para 4 | Within fingerprint range |\\n| The line / line refusal | paras 2, 9 | Recurring symbol |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## CROSS-CHAPTER VOICE CONSISTENCY\\n\\nChapter 5 maintains strong continuity with chapters 1–4:\\n\\n- **Sentence-length distribution**: varied (19–22 word mean range) ✓\\n- **Paragraph rhythm**: ~40% single-sentence paragraphs ✓\\n- **Dialogue-to-narrative ratio**: minimal dialogue, consistent with register ✓\\n- **Punctuation**: em dashes at estimated 2, zero semicolons, zero ellipses ✓\\n- **Metaphor domains**: sea as moral agent, weight/gravity, procedure as emotional defense ✓\\n- **Absence patterns**: no internal monologue in quoted form, no italics for emphasis, no abstractions for emotion ✓\\n\\n### Voice drift check: **NONE DETECTED**\\n\\nThis chapter could be dropped into the manuscript without any marker distinguishing it from chapters 1–4. The maritime procedural register is fully intact.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## TENSION STRUCTURE — CHAPTER 5\\n\\nThe chapter moves through procedural discovery:\\n1. **Skiff arrival** (no oars — forced arrival) → transactional dread (\\\"the way a bill arrives\\\")\\n2. **Knot observation** (tied wet) → inference about haste, abandonment\\n3. **Contradiction discovery** (the skiff was Kova's / Kova sold her) → two things true at once\\n4. **Tin discovery** (empty, marked) → someone was here, took contents, leaves message\\n5. **Refusal of closure** (line not drawn) → procedural rupture continues\\n\\nEach beat tightens. The chapter has momentum without rushing.\\n\\n---\\n\\n*End of Line Edit Report — Chapter 5 (Second Pass)*\",\"documentType\":\"LINE_EDIT_REPORT\",\"chapterNumber\":5},\"toolUseId\":\"call-baaeab84-622e-4510-b6e5-4261d39d12f8\"}}"
